# The job the next experiment/c2-serving-vN tag runs (.github/workflows/qwen-c2-serving.yml).
# C2_ACTIONS: any of status platform unserve priority reset cardm drift build probe smoke gate prefix replay push, in that order
# (fabric, quad only, runs between reset and cardm)
# (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses this file and refuses what the workflow must not act on).
#
# cardm: card B is reserved for another agent, so the single-card qualification harnesses (the card-B job's kind,
# .github/card-b-job.env) run on CARD M ALONE through this job, in the qwen-two-p150a-exclusive group. The step
# refuses first, as the gate does, while anything but tt-smi holds card M or card A, or a platform serving
# container (thatch-inference-*) exists; then it runs the harness with QUAL_CARD=blackhole-CEF5729692C19E6D
# (card M's board id) and ALLOW_SERVING_CARD=1, RESULTS set by the step, and C2_CARDM_ARGS as CARD_B_ARGS. The
# harness maps card M's node only, refuses while any container can reach any Tenstorrent device (a card-B job's
# container included: queue cardm when card B's runner is idle) and never resets; the step never touches card A
# or card B. After a hang, put reset (card M and card A together) before the next job that opens the pair. Its
# reports, logs and watcher log (not its kernel cache) are uploaded under cardm/ in the c2-serving artifact.
# C2_CARDM_HARNESS: a .sh under optimisation/ttnn-op/<dir>/ that embeds scripts/ci/qual_card.sh (required with
#   cardm; checked whenever set).
# C2_CARDM_ARGS: extra harness arguments, plain words (no quotes, globs or shell characters).
# C2_CARDM_ENV: extra environment, space-separated NAME=value; never QUAL_*, ALLOW_SERVING_CARD, RESULTS,
#   CARD_B_ARGS, PATH, HOME, BASH*, LD_*, DOCKER_* or SUDO_*.
# The K64j CB2a passes (s2-design.md W10a, 6.2) on graft K64j, watcher first: C2_ACTIONS=cardm, with
#   C2_CARDM_HARNESS=optimisation/ttnn-op/k64j/run_card_b.sh
#   (a) WATCHER pass: C2_CARDM_ARGS=--sections K2,X7,Z
#       C2_CARDM_ENV=WATCHER=1 KOPGRAFT64=/home/thatch/opgraft-K64j EXPECT_TTNNCPP_SHA256=<K64J_TTNNCPP_SHA256>
#       (K2 reads k2_verdict=REDUCED-PASS k2_coverage=38/1980 at best: never the policy's PASS)
#   (b) full pass: C2_CARDM_ARGS=--sections K2,X7,Z --seeds 0,1,2,3,4 --variants normal,peaky --no-timing
#       C2_CARDM_ENV=KOPGRAFT64=/home/thatch/opgraft-K64j EXPECT_TTNNCPP_SHA256=<K64J_TTNNCPP_SHA256>
#       (k2_verdict=PASS needs k2_coverage=1980/1980; K2's verdict sets the exactness policy's branch)
#
# C2_CARDS: the card set the hardware steps open. pair (the default): cards M and A, the (1, 2) mesh every pair profile
# opens. quad: every Blackhole board present as one (1, 4) mesh - the general-tp4 profiles (mesh_device P150x4) - with
# reset taking all four together (links train only at board init and the fabric is a full mesh), fabric running the
# four-card fabric probe, and gate and prefix mounting all four. quad refuses cardm, smoke, replay and priority (they
# are pair-shaped) and any profile that does not open the (1, 4) mesh; pair refuses the TP4 profiles. C2_FABRIC:
# FABRIC_1D (default) or FABRIC_1D_RING, the fabric the probe opens the mesh under. The tag for a fabric-only job
# still names an image (the probe runs in it); the four-card reset and probe need no build of the checkout.
# The image actions:
# C2_IMAGE_TAG: the image is zot.thatch.local:5000/tt-vllm:qwen38-c2-<tag>.
# C2_PROFILE: any profile of scripts/ci/qwen_c2_profiles.json (general, exact, coding, c2, c2-gate);
# what smoke and gate serve. c2-gate is c2's environment at exact's engine and prompt limit (the c2
# bring-up at v235's shape); c2 caps prompts at 123136 so every answer keeps 8192 tokens of room.
# C2_SMOKE_TESTS: comma-separated subset of scripts/ci/c2_serving_smoke.py's tests, or empty for all.
C2_ACTIONS=status reset replay
C2_IMAGE_TAG=s2-6a10e85
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,coding,long_real_text,concurrent4
# C2_PLATFORM_IMAGE: the thatch-serving-tt image the replay action runs (Thatch.Server tt-serving-image.yml output).
C2_PLATFORM_IMAGE=zot.thatch.local:5000/thatch-serving-tt@sha256:a85d012c23b772f86465f01b893824035b499ccae683dabf53e3a11ff00d080a
# The gate action (scripts/ci/c2_serving_gate.py), in the node agent's container shape. C2_GATE_PLAN:
# bringup (4 x 131072 real text, 256 out, against v235's texts - run it with C2_PROFILE=exact first,
# then c2-gate: c2 itself refuses 131072-token prompts), matrix (C2_GATE_LENGTHS, one prompt length per
# user, empty for the G4 ladder 60,255,2047,2048,2049,4096,32768,60000,120000 with its top rung lowered to
# the profile's largest admitted prompt; answers up to C2_GATE_MAX_TOKENS, at most the profile's output
# ceiling and what the longest prompt leaves of the context; solo vs concurrent under the exactness
# policy), memory (G5: 4 x the profile's largest prompt, or C2_GATE_MEMORY_PROMPT, x what the contract
# leaves it; on c2 and c2-gate also 4 x 60-token prompts x the whole ceiling), lifecycle (a drop during
# the engine build, drops at 4/3/2 live users, a triple drop
# in one round, a cancel during a 60k prefill, max_tokens=1, ignore_eos, freed slots, against a solo arm).
# matrix, memory and lifecycle need an image whose fast path takes any prompt length (S1). The gate
# refuses, before any container, lengths or budgets the image's profile cannot serve, and a plan list
# that may not finish in the time the step and job leave (matrix and lifecycle each fill most of a run).
# Comma-separated plans run in order. Put reset before gate after any failed run.
C2_GATE_PLAN=lifecycle
C2_GATE_LENGTHS=
C2_GATE_MAX_TOKENS=4096
C2_GATE_MEMORY_PROMPT=
# S2 gate keys (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py docstring; empty renders the gate's default).
C2_GATE_PAIRS=
C2_GATE_FAMILIES=
C2_GATE_JIT=
C2_GATE_POLICY=
C2_GATE_POLICY_DECISION=
C2_GATE_AUDITS=
# The prefix action (scripts/ci/c2_prefix_gate.py; TT prefix-reuse design 2.2, G1): C2_PREFIX_PLAN any of
# bringup exactness lifecycle timing, run in order (each fills much of a run: one or two per tag);
# C2_PREFIX_PROFILE the prefix-reuse profile (empty: general-prefix, which must be in the profiles);
# C2_PREFIX_BASELINE the no-reuse profile (empty: general; none drops timing's baseline arm);
# C2_PREFIX_AGENTS the timing phases' busy agents (empty: 1,4,5,6).
# The C2_PREFIX_* keys are read only when C2_ACTIONS has prefix.
C2_PREFIX_PLAN=timing
C2_PREFIX_PROFILE=general-prefix
C2_PREFIX_BASELINE=general
C2_PREFIX_AGENTS=1,4,5,6
# C2_REPLAY_PROFILE: the profile the replay's container serves (empty: the source container's).
C2_REPLAY_PROFILE=c2-packed
# C2_REPLAY_SERVED_MODEL: the model id (org/name[:tag]) the replay's /v1/models must advertise, without
# the checkpoint beside it, and every request after the warmup names. Empty: the replay's default,
# Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B:tt (the image's THATCH_SERVING_MODEL_ALIAS). An image built before the alias
# advertises the checkpoint: replay it with C2_REPLAY_SERVED_MODEL=Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B.
C2_REPLAY_SERVED_MODEL=
# The cardm action (see the top of this file); inert unless C2_ACTIONS names cardm. Set to CB2a's WATCHER pass.
C2_CARDM_HARNESS=optimisation/ttnn-op/k64j/run_card_b.sh
C2_CARDM_ARGS=--sections R1,S,R2,R4 --seeds 0,1,2 --variants normal,peaky
C2_CARDM_ENV=K64J_HARNESS=extent_reader KOPGRAFT64=/home/thatch/opgraft-K64j EXPECT_TTNNCPP_SHA256=152951c1c0de5c9dfad2d62c295393a43b2ecf353965c55c709da7e539b975b7
